Compute refers to the processing power needed to run applications, manage data and perform calculations.
Essentially, compute in the cloude means creating virtual machines with a cloud provider to run applications and tasks over the 
internet. In AWS, the VM is Amazon Elastic Comupute Cloud EC2. EC2 is flexible, cost effective and quick compared to buying your 
own on prem server and running installation.
With EC2 you only pay for running instances. VMs share an underlying physical host machine with other multiple instances and this
concept is called multitenancy. The VMs are isolated by a software called hypervisor which is running on the host machine.
If the application running is starting to max out the server, the server can be given more CPU and more memory (vertical scalling)
